      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Revolution refers to the movement of the Earth around the Sun.",
        "Leap Year adjustments account for the full duration of Earth's revolution cycle.",
        "Understanding the full rule of a Leap Year is essential for calendar calculations."
      ],
      "id": "115r1k4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m2mvh6i",
      "content": "• Divisible by 4 → Leap year."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Competitive exams frequently test the exact mathematical rule for identifying century leap years.",
        "Distinguish between Earth's rotation (day and night) and revolution (years and seasons)."
      ],
      "id": "e4z4yz4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yaxb4p6",
      "content": "• Century year must be divisible by 400."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7tt8egx",
      "content": "• Example: 2000 leap; 1900 not."
    }
